    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under realistic conditions. It is designed to catch silent failures \u2014 the most dangerous class of bugs in distributed systems, where requests complete successfully but with degraded quality, incorrect outputs, or unmeasured performance regressions.\n\n**How to use this checklist:** Each item should be executed and explicitly marked PASS, FAIL, or NOT APPLICABLE (with justification). \"NOT APPLICABLE\" without justification is treated as FAIL. Items marked with \u26a0 are commonly skipped in practice and deserve extra scrutiny.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove that every node in the cluster is running the exact same logical configuration, and that the configuration matches what you believe you deployed.\n\n### 1.1 Model and Weights\n- [ ] **1.1.1** Record the model identifier, revision/commit hash, and weight file checksums (SHA-256) on **every node**. Verify all nodes report identical values.\n- [ ] **1.1.2** \u26a0 Verify weight sharding is consistent: for tensor-parallel deployments, confirm each rank holds the correct shard by comparing a deterministic function of the shard (e.g., checksum of the shard tensor) against expected values derived from the full checkpoint.\n- [ ] **1.1.3** Verify dtype configuration (fp16/bf16/int8/fp8) is identical across nodes and matches the intended deployment spec. A single node silently falling back to fp32 or quantizing differently will produce subtly wrong outputs.\n- [ ] **1.1.4** Verify tokenizer files (vocab, merges, special tokens) are byte-identical across all nodes. Tokenizer drift between nodes causes inconsistent prompt processing in pipeline-parallel setups.\n-",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
